WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
 

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.037
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.037 --> 00:00:02.440
 

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.731
DAVE WILLIAMS: A common
challenge for improvement teams

00:00:04.731 --> 00:00:10.211
is identifying what changes you can
test to improve a process or problem.

00:00:10.211 --> 00:00:13.771
One great method to help you
break down ideas is a tool known

00:00:13.771 --> 00:00:16.031
as a "cause-and-effect diagram."

00:00:16.031 --> 00:00:19.761
You may have also heard of this tool
referred to as an "Ishikawa diagram"--

00:00:19.761 --> 00:00:23.731
attributed to its creator, Kaouru
Ishikawa-- or a "fishbone diagram"

00:00:23.731 --> 00:00:26.221
because of the resemblance
to the bones of a fish.

00:00:26.221 --> 00:00:28.581
To create a cause-and-effect
diagram, write

00:00:28.581 --> 00:00:31.671
the effect in a box on the
right-hand side of the page.

00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:35.111
So let's imagine we're working
on improving hand-washing.

00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:45.931
 

00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:46.461
All right.

00:00:46.461 --> 00:00:50.186
Then draw a horizontal
line across the page.

00:00:50.186 --> 00:00:53.421
 

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:57.421
Decide on a few categories
or causes for the problem.

00:00:57.421 --> 00:01:00.641
Useful categories of causes in
the classic fishbone diagram

00:01:00.641 --> 00:01:09.569
include people, methods, materials,
equipment, and environment.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.341
 

00:01:12.341 --> 00:01:16.131
Then we can draw a diagonal
line to each of these,

00:01:16.131 --> 00:01:20.766
and these are actually the bones
of the fish-- and hence, its name.

00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:26.041
 

00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:28.761
The process of categorizing
potential causes

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:33.171
may be very useful to help you
to break down a complex problem

00:01:33.171 --> 00:01:37.531
and focus in on it from
various perspectives.

00:01:37.531 --> 00:01:39.801
So as you're looking at
each of the categories,

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:42.281
you want to generate a list of causes.

00:01:42.281 --> 00:01:46.435
In this example, people
might include clinical staff.

00:01:46.435 --> 00:01:49.953
 

00:01:49.953 --> 00:01:50.453
All right.

00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:52.391
It also might include
non-clinical staff.

00:01:52.391 --> 00:01:57.001
 

00:01:57.001 --> 00:01:59.841
Let's put them as just "other staff."

00:01:59.841 --> 00:02:01.181
It might include the methods.

00:02:01.181 --> 00:02:03.729
How do you actually wash your hands?

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:06.931
 

00:02:06.931 --> 00:02:09.871
I'll say "wash process."

00:02:09.871 --> 00:02:11.181
It could be the materials.

00:02:11.181 --> 00:02:15.301
Are you using the right kind of
soap, or does it dry out your hands?

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.565
So we'll think about the soap.

00:02:18.565 --> 00:02:20.481
It could be the equipment,
like the dispenser.

00:02:20.481 --> 00:02:23.531
 

00:02:23.531 --> 00:02:25.211
Is there an easy dispenser to use?

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.381
Does it give you the right amount?

00:02:27.381 --> 00:02:29.931
Or maybe it's the environment.

00:02:29.931 --> 00:02:32.691
Where is the dispenser location?

00:02:32.691 --> 00:02:35.511
Is it near the process of care?

00:02:35.511 --> 00:02:40.661
Identify the causes by asking why with
people that are closest to the process

00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:43.481
until you've reached a
useful level of detail.

00:02:43.481 --> 00:02:47.631
That is when the cause is specific
enough to be able to test a change

00:02:47.631 --> 00:02:49.261
and to measure its effects.

00:02:49.261 --> 00:02:51.651
Sometimes, I like to describe
this for folks that have

00:02:51.651 --> 00:02:54.381
children as the five-year-old method.

00:02:54.381 --> 00:02:58.653
If you ever had a kid, they
asked you "why" five times

00:02:58.653 --> 00:03:00.861
constantly until they get
to the root of the problem.

00:03:00.861 --> 00:03:03.461
And you're doing the same thing here.

00:03:03.461 --> 00:03:16.682
 

